      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All tasks completed. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**1. Living room devices found (4):** `lock_main`, `light_living`, `ac_living`, `tv_living`\\n\\n**2. Health diagnosis (all_issues criterion):** 0 abnormal devices — everything is healthy. One caveat worth flagging: the `lock_main` status in the diagnosis data was `locked`, which isn't an issue type, so the lock's lock state doesn't appear to have triggered a health alert. If you expected a fault to surface, the diagnosis ran against a flat device list rather than a per-device status feed, so no device-level health data was available to verify.\\n\\n**3. Light (`light_living`):** Initially the light-request tool returned a mismatched device (`light_bedroom`) with a pending state, so I re-ran the power state set on `light_living` (executed) and the brightness update (executed). Final result: on at 70% brightness.\\n\\n**4. Lock (`lock_main`):** Applied `lock` state with PIN 2026 — confirmed `new_state: locked`, status `executed`.\\n\\n**5. Alert:** High-priority app notification sent to `default_user` (ID `NOTIFEE84C`) titled \\\"IoT Remediation Summary\\\" with the backup `iot_security_run` saved in `/projects` (Backup ID `BACKUPA3B2C`, 190 MB, status completed, note `NOTE18E3D`).\"}\n</action>",
